  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Solve for $x\\in[0,2\\pi)$. Answer in exact form if possible, otherwise round to 3 d.p.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=\\sec x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,\\pi$",
          "worked": "Using $\\sec x=\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$, where $\\cos x\\ne0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x&=\\frac{1}{\\cos x}\\\\\\cos^2x&=1\\\\\\cos x&=\\pm1.\\end{align*}$$\nOn $[0,2\\pi)$, $x=0,\\pi$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 33
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2x=\\cos x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2x-\\cos x&=0\\\\\\cos x(\\cos x-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\cos x=0$ or $\\cos x=1$.\n\nFor $\\cos x=0$, $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.\n\nFor $\\cos x=1$, $x=0$ on the given domain.\n\nTherefore $x=0,\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(2\\sin x+1)(3\\cos x-1)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1.231,\\frac{7\\pi}{6},5.052,\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$",
          "worked": "$2\\sin x+1=0$ or $3\\cos x-1=0$.\n\nFor the first factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin x&=-\\frac12\\\\A&=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac12\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{6}.\\end{align*}$$\nSine is negative in Q3 and Q4, so $x=\\frac{7\\pi}{6},\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$.\n\nFor the second factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos x&=\\frac13\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac13\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is positive in Q1 and Q4, so $x=A$ or $2\\pi-A$.\n\nTherefore $x=1.231,\\frac{7\\pi}{6},5.052,\\frac{11\\pi}{6}$, with decimal answers rounded to 3 d.p.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x+3\\cot x-4=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},1.249,\\frac{5\\pi}{4},4.391$",
          "worked": "Using $\\cot x=\\frac{1}{\\tan x}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan x+\\frac{3}{\\tan x}-4&=0\\\\\\tan^2x-4\\tan x+3&=0\\\\(\\tan x-1)(\\tan x-3)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\tan x=1$ or $\\tan x=3$.\n\nTangent is positive in Q1 and Q3.\n\nFor $\\tan x=1$, $A=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$, giving $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.\n\nFor $\\tan x=3$, $A=\\tan^{-1}(3)$, giving $x=A,A+\\pi$.\n\nTherefore $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},1.249,\\frac{5\\pi}{4},4.391$, with decimal answers rounded to 3 d.p.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin^2x+3\\sin x-2=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin^2x+3\\sin x-2&=0\\\\(2\\sin x-1)(\\sin x+2)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\sin x=\\frac{1}{2}$ or $\\sin x=-2$.\n\nReject $\\sin x=-2$, since $-1\\le\\sin x\\le1$.\n\nFor $\\sin x=\\frac{1}{2}$, the reference angle is $A=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Sine is positive in Q1 and Q2.\n\nTherefore $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{5\\pi}{6}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$6\\sin x\\cos^2x-2\\sin x=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,0.955,2.186,\\pi,4.097,5.328$",
          "worked": "$$2\\sin x(3\\cos^2x-1)=0.$$\nThus $\\sin x=0$ or $3\\cos^2x-1=0$.\n\nFor $\\sin x=0$, $x=0,\\pi$ on the given domain.\n\nFor the other factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\cos^2x-1&=0\\\\\\cos^2x&=\\frac13\\\\\\cos x&=\\pm\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nThe two signs give solutions in all four quadrants:\n$$x=A,\\ \\pi-A,\\ \\pi+A,\\ 2\\pi-A.$$\nTherefore $x=0,0.955,2.186,\\pi,4.097,5.328$, with decimal answers rounded to 3 d.p.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
